From 7e36a37547903bf50a2ecd7710295d4eb19aaf0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?C=C3=BCneyt=20=C4=B0nan?= <cuneytinan37@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:51:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add Mateless: material test, lock detector and Domino
 search

Three rungs that prove a side can never be mated (FIDE 5.2.2, 6.9), in
package chess.mateless; no behaviour of scalachess changes:

- Material: the other side lacks the material to mate at all.
- Lock: pawns, kings and bishops form a structure that no series of
  legal moves can open (a bitboard fixed point, no move generated).
- Domino: a 6-ply, 100-node helpmate search without move-count rules,
  asking the two static tests after the moves that can change them.

Ladder gives the proofs for one position (proveCannotBeMated, proveBoth,
isDead, opponentCannotMate); Flags keeps a game's two "may still mate"
flags ply by ply.

Moves are tried in Mateless's order, so proofs, failures and node counts
are those of Mateless's JavaScript and Rust engines: identical on
chasolver's 68,950 positions, 192,457 Lichess timeouts and 250k games.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CNt12HAZEwEiCouRmksRvj
